Filed by the WindowsAgent (Claude on Getty's Windows PC, MARSUPILAMI 10.5.10.12) on 2026-11-11, at Getty's request: what the Windows side expects from the HQ rollout. homelab steers the rollout (CA, vendor install on pikachu, device list); this card only says what has to be true at the client.

Why: Getty opens the HQ web consoles from MARSUPILAMI in MobaXterm browser sessions (Edge WebView2 157), Chrome app windows (Chrome 157) and Firefox 159. Every one of them shows a certificate warning today, and Chromium does not offer to save a password on a page with a certificate error - so no console remembers its login.

The consoles, by the URL in use (measured 2026-11-11 with openssl s_client from MARSUPILAMI):

| URL | Device | Presents today | Way in SICK |
|---|---|---|---|
| https://kaiser.cihq:8006/ | PVE 9.2, kaiser (R720xd) | its own PVE cluster CA, SAN kaiser.cihq | proxmox-ve |
| https://bigbird.cihq:8006/ | PVE 9.2, bigbird | another PVE cluster CA, SAN bigbird.cihq | proxmox-ve |
| https://snorlax.cihq:8007/ | PBS 4.2, snorlax | self-signed, SAN snorlax.cihq | proxmox-bs |
| https://kaiser-idrac.cihq/ | iDRAC 7, FW 2.65 | Dell factory cert CN=idrac-7BKMT02, no SAN | k18 |
| https://grafana.k8s.cihq/ | k8s gateway 10.5.10.64 | cert-manager wildcard *.k8s.cihq from cihq-ca | cert-manager from the SICK CA |

ha.hq.srv.ci has a Let's Encrypt certificate and is out of scope.

Expected:
1. One root for all of them. The k8s gateway moves from cihq-ca to the SICK CA (k8s/cert-manager), so cihq-ca never has to be trusted on a client.
2. Each certificate carries the name in the URL above (more names are homelab's choice), and the server sends leaf + intermediate.
3. Proxmox VE: only the custom certificate changes (pveproxy-ssl.pem, what proxmox-ve uploads); pve-ssl.pem and the cluster CA stay. The SPICE links in Getty's start menu (WindowsAgent VMs\spice.ps1: porygon VM 200 on bigbird, machoke VM 151 on kaiser) put the cluster CA from `pvesh create /nodes/<node>/qemu/<vmid>/spiceproxy` into the .vv file and must keep working.
4. Renewal needs nobody at the PC; at most the console reloads.
5. The iDRAC follows when k18 is settled; its password is unknown today (note on k18).

Done when, checked by the WindowsAgent from MARSUPILAMI with the root installed (k78): every URL above opens without a warning in a MobaXterm Edge session, Chrome and Firefox; `Invoke-WebRequest` in Windows PowerShell 5.1 succeeds without skipping the certificate check; Chrome offers to save the login; the porygon and machoke SPICE links still connect. The WindowsAgent then switches its MobaXterm web sessions to https (Grafana is http there today) and writes the result on this card.

